        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Reginald Engelbach, Christiane Desroches Noblecourt\n- Places: Cairo, Harageh, Egypt\n- Organizations: Egyptian Museum of Cairo\n- Roles: Egyptologist, engineer\n\nFacts:\n- Reginald Engelbach was born on July 9, 1888, and he was an English Egyptologist and engineer.\n- Reginald Engelbach excavated the cemeteries at Harageh in 1913.\n- Christiane Desroches Noblecourt was born on November 17, 1913, and she was a French Egyptologist.\n- Reginald Engelbach is mainly known for his work at the Egyptian Museum of Cairo, especially for compiling a register of the museum's artifacts.\n- Cairo is the capital and largest city of Egypt.\n- Reginald Engelbach died on February 26, 1946.\n- Christiane Desroches Noblecourt died on June 23, 2011.",
